{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-127142" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the flux of the vector field $F(x,y)=7\\,i+2\\,j$ across the circle $C$ with equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=36.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074644/state.json" "file_sha256" "035a175eafdd7822c1d888681f760049d681a709c869d2382c55ec0af7ab930e"} {"question" "q-127142" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field and $C$ is a piecewise-smooth, simple, closed curve, then the flux of $F$ across $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}y-Q\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ denotes the outward-pointing unit normal vector to $C.$ \n\nThe closed curve $C$ is a circle centered at the origin with the radius $6.$ It can be parameterized in the counterclockwise direction as\n\n$$\nr(t)=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,0\\le t\\le 2\\pi .\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x,y) & =7, \\\\ Q(x,y) & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x(t)$ and $y(t)$ along the curve, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)=-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}y-Q\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(P\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}-Q\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(7)\\cdot (6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)-(2)\\cdot (-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }42\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+12\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(42\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-12\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =(0-12)-(0-12) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074644/state.json" "file_sha256" "035a175eafdd7822c1d888681f760049d681a709c869d2382c55ec0af7ab930e"} {"question" "q-127142" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074644/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0287a99bcb35f7748844b4766793b222a551470ce220e8d5df6c3d2c6ce985c1"} {"question" "q-127142" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074644/state.json" "file_sha256" "035a175eafdd7822c1d888681f760049d681a709c869d2382c55ec0af7ab930e"} {"question" "q-127142" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "24"] ["math" "30"] ["math" "54"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074644/state.json" "file_sha256" "035a175eafdd7822c1d888681f760049d681a709c869d2382c55ec0af7ab930e"} {"question" "q-127142" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074644/state.json" "file_sha256" "035a175eafdd7822c1d888681f760049d681a709c869d2382c55ec0af7ab930e"} {"question" "q-127148" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the flux of the vector field $F(x,y)=8\\,i-(x+3)\\,j$ across the circle $C$ with equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074644/state.json" "file_sha256" "035a175eafdd7822c1d888681f760049d681a709c869d2382c55ec0af7ab930e"} {"question" "q-127148" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field and $C$ is a piecewise-smooth, simple, closed curve, then the flux of $F$ across $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}y-Q\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ denotes the outward-pointing unit normal vector to $C.$ \n\nFirst, we write the equation of our curve as\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={2}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe closed curve $C$ is a circle centered at the origin with the radius $2.$ It can be parameterized in the counterclockwise direction as\n\n$$\nr(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,0\\le t\\le 2\\pi .\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x,y) & =8, \\\\ Q(x,y) & =x+3=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x(t)$ and $y(t)$ along the curve, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral using the double-angle formula for sine, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}y-Q\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(P\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}-Q\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(8)\\cdot (2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)-(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-3)\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }16\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }16\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(16\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074644/state.json" "file_sha256" "035a175eafdd7822c1d888681f760049d681a709c869d2382c55ec0af7ab930e"} {"question" "q-127148" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074644/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0287a99bcb35f7748844b4766793b222a551470ce220e8d5df6c3d2c6ce985c1"} {"question" "q-127148" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074644/state.json" "file_sha256" "035a175eafdd7822c1d888681f760049d681a709c869d2382c55ec0af7ab930e"} {"question" "q-127148" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "2\\pi "] ["math" "4\\pi "] ["math" "5\\pi "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074644/state.json" "file_sha256" "035a175eafdd7822c1d888681f760049d681a709c869d2382c55ec0af7ab930e"} {"question" "q-127148" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074644/state.json" "file_sha256" "035a175eafdd7822c1d888681f760049d681a709c869d2382c55ec0af7ab930e"} {"question" "q-127151" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074644/assets/0ea0204d3e1f230efcde4b82da36b1986af732cdf2a01ad868aa0f6bf7414326.png)\n\nCalculate the flux of the vector field $F(x,y)=4y\\,i+(2x-1)\\,j$ through the curve $C$ given by $r(t)={t}^{2}\\,i+t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,1],$ measured with respect to the unit normal vector $n$ on $C,$ as shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074644/state.json" "file_sha256" "035a175eafdd7822c1d888681f760049d681a709c869d2382c55ec0af7ab930e"} {"question" "q-127151" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field and $C$ is a piecewise-smooth, simple curve, then the flux of $F$ across $C$ measured with respect to a unit normal vector $n$ on $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{C}P\\,\\text{d}y-Q\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo apply this formula, \n\n- the curve should be parameterized as $r(t)$ for $t\\in [a,b],$ and\n\n- the unit normal vector $n$ *must* be a ${90}^{∘}$ clockwise rotation of the unit tangent vector $T(t).$\n\nIn this case, $n$ is indeed a ${90}^{∘}$ clockwise rotation of $T,$ so we can apply the above formula. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074644/assets/59e503e0c4d950f030891bbaeb7ed890426ef470a1e1dae89d27eabb8dd591a6.png)\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx={t}^{2},\\,y=t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x,y) & =4y=4t, \\\\ Q(x,y) & =2x-1=2{t}^{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x(t)$ and $y(t)$ along the curve, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})=2t, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{C}P\\,\\text{d}y-Q\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(P\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}-Q\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(4t)\\cdot (1)-(2{t}^{2}-1)\\cdot (2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4t-4{t}^{3}+2t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6t-4{t}^{3}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}-{t}^{4}{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(3-1)-(0-0){|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074644/state.json" "file_sha256" "035a175eafdd7822c1d888681f760049d681a709c869d2382c55ec0af7ab930e"} {"question" "q-127151" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074644/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0287a99bcb35f7748844b4766793b222a551470ce220e8d5df6c3d2c6ce985c1"} {"question" "q-127151" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074644/state.json" "file_sha256" "035a175eafdd7822c1d888681f760049d681a709c869d2382c55ec0af7ab930e"} {"question" "q-127151" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074644/state.json" "file_sha256" "035a175eafdd7822c1d888681f760049d681a709c869d2382c55ec0af7ab930e"} {"question" "q-127151" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074644/state.json" "file_sha256" "035a175eafdd7822c1d888681f760049d681a709c869d2382c55ec0af7ab930e"} {"question" "q-127244" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074644/assets/6043a1f88474e2c282938d3b3f0193002b6e11b5fb6d16292fea43d63292d1b0.png)\n\nThe curve $C$ is given by $y={x}^{3}$ from the point $(0,0)$ to the point $(1,1).$ Calculate the flux of the vector field $F(x,y)=-3{x}^{2}\\,i+\\,j$ through $C,$ measured with respect to the unit normal vector $n$ on $C,$ as shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074644/state.json" "file_sha256" "035a175eafdd7822c1d888681f760049d681a709c869d2382c55ec0af7ab930e"} {"question" "q-127244" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field and $C$ is a piecewise-smooth, simple curve, then the flux of $F$ across $C$ measured with respect to a unit normal vector $n$ on $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{C}P\\,\\text{d}y-Q\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo apply this formula, \n\n- the curve should be parameterized as $r(t)$ for $t\\in [a,b],$ and\n\n- the unit normal vector $n$ *must* be a ${90}^{∘}$ clockwise rotation of the unit tangent vector $T(t).$\n\nParameterizing the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=t,\\,y={t}^{3},\\,t\\in [0,1].\n$$\n\n \n\nThis parameterization traverses the curve from the point $(0,0)$ to the point $(1,1).$ Therefore, $n$ is indeed a ${90}^{∘}$ clockwise rotation of $T,$ so we can apply the above formula for the flux. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074644/assets/1d54fe3c07f04a7d05567942e3eea6efaf1cb516070a5d7cc31ef726c0ddb423.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x,y) & =-3{x}^{2}=-3{t}^{2}, \\\\ Q(x,y) & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x(t)$ and $y(t)$ along the curve, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)=1, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})=3{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{C}P\\,\\text{d}y-Q\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(P\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}-Q\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-3{t}^{2})\\cdot (3{t}^{2})-(1)\\cdot (1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}-9{t}^{4}-1\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(-\\frac{9{t}^{5}}{5}-t){|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(-\\frac{9}{5}-1)-0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{14}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074644/state.json" "file_sha256" "035a175eafdd7822c1d888681f760049d681a709c869d2382c55ec0af7ab930e"} {"question" "q-127244" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074644/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0287a99bcb35f7748844b4766793b222a551470ce220e8d5df6c3d2c6ce985c1"} {"question" "q-127244" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074644/state.json" "file_sha256" "035a175eafdd7822c1d888681f760049d681a709c869d2382c55ec0af7ab930e"} {"question" "q-127244" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{14}{5}"] ["math" "-\\frac{7}{5}"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "\\frac{14}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074644/state.json" "file_sha256" "035a175eafdd7822c1d888681f760049d681a709c869d2382c55ec0af7ab930e"} {"question" "q-127244" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{14}{5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074644/state.json" "file_sha256" "035a175eafdd7822c1d888681f760049d681a709c869d2382c55ec0af7ab930e"} {"question" "q-127254" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074644/assets/67dca8f0202d0c5d1041935a6aee7c4ebd0e3c6c449f2ee1a5ff24c1f381410c.png)\n\nThe curve $C$ is given by $x=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡y$ from the point $(1,\\frac{1}{e})$ to the point $(0,1).$ Calculate the flux of the vector field $F(x,y)=2{y}^{2}\\,j$ through $C,$ measured with respect to the unit normal vector $n$ on $C,$ as shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074644/state.json" "file_sha256" "035a175eafdd7822c1d888681f760049d681a709c869d2382c55ec0af7ab930e"} {"question" "q-127254" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field and $C$ is a piecewise-smooth, simple curve, then the flux of $F$ across $C$ measured with respect to a unit normal vector $n$ on $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{C}P\\,\\text{d}y-Q\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo apply this formula, \n\n- the curve should be parameterized as $r(t)$ for $t\\in [a,b],$ and\n\n- the unit normal vector $n$ *must* be a ${90}^{∘}$ clockwise rotation of the unit tangent vector $T(t).$\n\nParameterizing the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,y=t,\\,t\\in [\\frac{1}{e},1].\n$$\n\n \n\nThis parameterization traverses the curve from the point $(1,\\frac{1}{e})$ to the point $(0,1).$ Therefore, $n$ is indeed a ${90}^{∘}$ clockwise rotation of $T,$ so we can apply the above formula for the flux. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074644/assets/08fc4561a322b690da7bd28a9e69a91c687256e8a902ec7690dda5e6a1c689a6.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x,y) & =0, \\\\ Q(x,y) & =2{y}^{2}=2{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x(t)$ and $y(t)$ along the curve, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)=-\\frac{1}{t}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{C}P\\,\\text{d}y-Q\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/e}^{1}(P\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}-Q\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/e}^{1}(0)\\cdot (1)-(2{t}^{2})\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{t})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/e}^{1}2t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =({t}^{2}){|}_{1/e}^{1} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074644/state.json" "file_sha256" "035a175eafdd7822c1d888681f760049d681a709c869d2382c55ec0af7ab930e"} {"question" "q-127254" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074644/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0287a99bcb35f7748844b4766793b222a551470ce220e8d5df6c3d2c6ce985c1"} {"question" "q-127254" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074644/state.json" "file_sha256" "035a175eafdd7822c1d888681f760049d681a709c869d2382c55ec0af7ab930e"} {"question" "q-127254" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "1+\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}"] ["math" "1+{e}^{2}"] ["math" "1-\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}"] ["math" "1-{e}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074644/state.json" "file_sha256" "035a175eafdd7822c1d888681f760049d681a709c869d2382c55ec0af7ab930e"} {"question" "q-127254" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1-\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074644/state.json" "file_sha256" "035a175eafdd7822c1d888681f760049d681a709c869d2382c55ec0af7ab930e"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2746 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
